---
const stages = [
  {
    step: '1',
    when: '~May 2026',
    who: 'Internal OpenAI reasoning model',
    what: 'Produces a counterexample argument',
    detail:
      'A general-purpose reasoning model, not a mathematics-specialised system. Reported to succeed on roughly half of attempts at maximum token budget.',
    status: 'machine output'
  },
  {
    step: '2',
    when: '20 May 2026',
    who: 'OpenAI writeup',
    what: 'Published as a preprint on openai.com',
    detail:
      'States: there is an absolute constant delta > 0 and infinitely many n with at least n^(1+delta) unit distances. The constant is not made explicit.',
    status: 'informal prose'
  },
  {
    step: '3',
    when: '20 May 2026',
    who: 'Nine mathematicians',
    what: 'Human-verified digest and reflections',
    detail:
      'Alon, Bloom, Gowers, Litt, Sawin, Shankar, Tsimerman, Wang and Matchett Wood compress the argument and locate its ancestry in Golod-Shafarevich, Hajir-Maire-Ramakrishna and Ellenberg-Venkatesh.',
    status: 'referee-grade reading'
  },
  {
    step: '4',
    when: '20 May 2026',
    who: 'Will Sawin, independently',
    what: 'Makes the exponent explicit',
    detail:
      'A separate preprint proves more than n^1.014 unit-distance pairs, using the same Golod-Shafarevich route to number fields of large degree and small discriminant.',
    status: 'human extension'
  },
  {
    step: '5',
    when: 'June 2026',
    who: 'Certificate optimisation, Aleph Prover',
    what: 'Sharper constants, then a Lean 4 check',
    detail:
      'Search over explicit prime certificates pushes delta past 0.03. A separate formalisation reaches a machine-checked proof of about 33,000 lines, conditional on two classical theorems still unformalised in Mathlib.',
    status: 'partially formal'
  }
]
---

<figure class="viz pipeline-viz" aria-labelledby="unit-distance-pipeline-title">
  <figcaption id="unit-distance-pipeline-title">
    <strong>From model output to machine-checked artefact</strong>
    <span>
      The result was announced and refereed on the same day, then sharpened and formalised over
      the following six weeks.
    </span>
  </figcaption>

  <ol class="stages">
    {
      stages.map((s) => (
        <li>
          <div class="head">
            <span class="step">{s.step}</span>
            <span class="when">{s.when}</span>
            <span class="status">{s.status}</span>
          </div>
          <strong>{s.what}</strong>
          <em>{s.who}</em>
          <p>{s.detail}</p>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <p class="foot">
    No stage is redundant. Step 3 is what turned an unrefereed PDF into something a
    combinatorialist could act on; step 5 is what makes the argument auditable without trusting
    any human reading at all.
  </p>
</figure>

<style>
  .viz {
    container-type: inline-size;
    margin: 2em 0;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--astro-code-background);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  figcaption {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.15rem;
  }
  figcaption strong {
    font: 600 var(--font-size-s) var(--mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  figcaption span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font: 0.7rem/1.5 var(--mono);
  }
  .stages {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .stages li {
    display: grid;
    align-content: start;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 0.8rem 0.75rem;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--text-secondary);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg);
  }
  .head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.35rem 0.5rem;
  }
  .step {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font: 600 0.62rem var(--mono);
  }
  .when {
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    font: 0.62rem var(--mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .status {
    padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    font: 0.58rem var(--mono);
  }
  .stages strong {
    font: 600 0.78rem/1.35 var(--sans);
  }
  .stages em {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font: 0.66rem/1.4 var(--mono);
    font-style: normal;
  }
  .stages p {
    margin: 0.1rem 0 0;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font: 0.64rem/1.55 var(--mono);
  }
  .foot {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    padding-top: 0.85rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font: 0.68rem/1.6 var(--mono);
  }
  @container (max-width: 780px) {
    .stages {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  @container (max-width: 480px) {
    .stages {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
